{number: 116}
{title: The God of Abraham Praise}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
The [C] God of Abraham [G] praise, who [C] reigns enthroned a-[G] bove;
Ancient of [C] everlasting days, and [F] God of [C] [G7] [C] love.
Jehovah, great I AM! by [G] earth and heav'n con-[C] fest;
I bow and [F] bless the [C] sacred Name, for-[G7] ever [C] blest.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
The [C] God of Abraham [G] praise, at [C] whose supreme com-[G] mand
From earth I [C] rise, and seek the joys at [F] His right [C] [G7] [C] hand:
I all on earth forsake, its [G] wisdom, fame, and [C] pow'r;
And Him my [F] only [C] portion make, my [G7] shield and [C] tow'r.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
He [C] by Himself hath [G] sworn, I [C] on His oath de-[G] pend,
I shall, on [C] eagle wings upborne, to [F] heav'n a-[C] [G7] [C] scend:
I shall behold His face, I [G] shall His pow'r a-[C] dore,
And sing the [F] wonders [C] of His grace for-[G7] ever-[C] more.
{end_of_verse}
